'''[[Nechryael]]''' are a type of demon that can be assigned as a slayer task at level 80 [[Slayer]] and 85 combat by various [[Slayer Master|Slayer masters]]. They are notable for their frequent drops of herbs, seeds, and alchable items, making them an extremely good slayer task.

Nechryael attack with melee, and can periodically summon up to two [[death spawn]]s to assist them in battle. These death spawns are fairly inaccurate with a max hit of 2, but as they attack with typeless melee, [[Protect from Melee]] has no effect on them. Uniquely, they are able to attack you in single-combat areas regardless of if you are already in combat. It is recommended to bring food if using Melee or to have runes to cast blood spells if using Magic to kill nechryaels. It is also possible to leave the area and return to lose aggression, but this is impractical in most situations.

A stronger variant of the Nechryael, the [[Greater Nechryael]], can be found in the [[Catacombs of Kourend]], [[Iorwerth Dungeon]] and [[Wilderness Slayer Cave]]. These are mechanically the same as their standard counterparts, barring higher stats. It is highly recommended to kill these whenever possible, as they have a more lucrative drop table. Both variants share the same superior, the [[Nechryarch]], though the common drop table takes from whichever variant they came from. Nechryarch attack with melee, but will periodically summon a trio of [[chaotic death spawn]]; one each in melee, magic and ranged. They hit significantly harder, but their attacks can be blocked with prayer. These spawns will only appear if the Nechryarch is allowed to attack the player, so using safespots or farcasting will prevent this from happening.

Players who seek a fast task are encouraged to kill them in the Catacombs of Kourend, as fourteen greater nechryael are found in two chambers of seven each. With a [[goading potion]] to draw aggression, players will find themselves gaining very high experience rates with minimal downtime. 

If not intending to mage greater nechryael, players are recommended to melee them in the Iorwerth Dungeon, as it is very likely to be crashed by another player if using melee in the catacombs. The nechryael in the dungeon are able to drop [[crystal shard]]s to increase overall profit per task.

If killing nechryael under an assignment from [[Krystilia]], players must head to the Wilderness Slayer Cave. A goading potion is recommended, along with a one-click teleport such as a [[royal seed pod]]. The player can easily teleport out of the dungeon, but the caves themselves are a very popular [[player killing]] spot and players are likely to die if they do not pay attention in the caves.

Normal nechryael yield lower Slayer experience rates, although for [[Ironman Mode|ironman players]] in particular, their more plentiful seed drops are a very efficient source for Herblore training and general potions. In addition, as they are roughly twice as fast to kill, their malicious ashes can be offered more frequently for higher Prayer experience rates. Most nechryael are found in the Slayer Tower, though they may also be found in the [[Charred Dungeon]], which is a [[multicombat area]]. It is highly encouraged to kill the normal nechryael here, as despite there only being 6 spawns, the significantly faster kill times and better seed drop rates make them a lucrative task as well as a good task for hunting the [[imbued heart]]. This dungeon requires 60 [[Sailing]] to access the island and is very close to [[Wyrmscraig]], allowing for reasonably quick access with a [[necklace of passage]] should the player not have a boat docked at charred island with a [[Greater teleport focus (facility)|greater teleport focus]].

